chaos.json / chaos-rules.json / chaos.words: gambit-finish with Gambit's vanilla stack-building taken out for chaos (run 4): no raise
(gambit-rules.json raises to row 11), no material floor (>=40 panels), no opener (an 8-chain by frame 600). Written the same way.
bench/play.sh plays profiles/${CHAOSBOT_PROFILE:-chaos}.words.

chaos.words (run 95, 2026-11-26): finish them asks combos 4, 5, 6 before 8, 9, 10 -- a four buys about 23 frames of freeze and stop
a panel, an eight about 15. The profile before it is chaos-big.words.
Run 96 (combos 4-6 first always): seeds 13-14 6/8. chaos.words is the eights-first profile again; the order is chosen each decision
by the panels on the board instead (decide.c, run 97): smallest first at or under the life peak (33 panels), as listed above it.

lineclear.words (run 244, 2026-11-28): chaos.words with the mode in force 3, "big chain", in place of 1, "finish them" (the profile line's
first number is answer.c gb_profile's modeRule: the mode played all game). A Line Clear stage is won by rows sent in two minutes with
no garbage coming (ChallengeMode.lua lineHeightToKill), and a chain sends rows where finish them's combos send half-rows.
lineclear.words, run 245: the mode in force 0, "time attack" (its chain designer, search/chainbuild.c) -- run 244's "big chain" won
15:3-4 (22-27 rows a minute) and held where no line met its list at 7 colours (15:5-6, 11-12 a minute, 71-89 holds a game).
lineclear.words, run 246: the mode in force 4, "pressure" (chains of 4 and 3 within 240 frames) -- run 245's time attack (chains of 8
and more) won 5/8 at 24-35 rows a minute; 15:6 asks 40, and the chains it threw (6-9 links) took too long to build.
lineclear.words, run 247: back to time attack (mode 0) -- run 246's pressure won 1/8 at 11-17 rows a minute.
lineclear.words, run 261: time attack's list (rule 0) is a chain of 8 or more, then a chain of 3 or more (was the 8 alone) -- at seven
colours no line came near 8, and the rank's lines between chains set up two-column combos (500-1000 frames a game in run 253's 15:5-6),
which send a row where a chain's link sends one each.
Run 261 (02:01 ET): won 4/8 -- worse; lineclear.words back to run 253's (3931d36).
